{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AAO REVIEWS - SERVER-RENDERED LIST (metaobject mode)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The metaobject-backed replacement for renderWidget() in assets/aao-reviews.js. Same DOM, same class
names, so assets/aao-reviews.css is unchanged and the widget looks identical to the JSON-driven one.

Where the reviews come from, in order:

  1. product.metafields.custom.aao_own_reviews   list.metaobject_reference -> aao_review
     The product's OWN reviews. Wins outright when present.
  2. product.metafields.custom.aao_review_group  metaobject_reference -> aao_review_group
     A shared group; its `reviews` list is used.

Reviews with `hidden = true` are skipped everywhere: cards, count, average, histogram and JSON-LD.

ORDER IS AUTHORING ORDER. The list field's order in the Shopify admin is the order shown on the
storefront, so the client reorders reviews by dragging. Nothing here sorts: Liquid cannot sort an
array of metaobjects by a nested field value reliably, and a drag handle is a better editing
experience than an invisible sort rule. The migration writes each list newest-first.

What the old JS did at runtime and Liquid now does at render time:

  * average, review count and the 1-5 histogram  (one pass over the list)
  * the first PAGE_SIZE cards visible, the rest server-rendered with `hidden` and revealed by
    assets/aao-reviews-mo.js on "Load more reviews"
  * Product / AggregateRating / Review JSON-LD, now in the HTML source instead of injected after
    paint, so crawlers that do not execute JS see it

********************************************
Supported variables
********************************************

* product:   the product to show reviews for. Required.
* heading:   optional heading text. Defaults to "Customer Reviews".
* max_width: optional px width. Defaults to 1080.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign rv_product = product
  assign rv_heading = heading | default: 'Customer Reviews'
  assign rv_max_width = max_width | default: 1080
  assign rv_page_size = 5
  assign rv_jsonld_max = 20

  assign rv_own = rv_product.metafields.custom.aao_own_reviews.value
  assign rv_group = rv_product.metafields.custom.aao_review_group.value

  assign rv_list = ''
  if rv_own != blank and rv_own.size > 0
    assign rv_list = rv_own
  elsif rv_group != blank and rv_group.reviews.value != blank
    assign rv_list = rv_group.reviews.value
  endif

  comment
    Pass 1: count, sum and histogram over the visible reviews. Liquid has no mutable arrays, so the
    five buckets are five variables.
  endcomment
  assign rv_count = 0
  assign rv_sum = 0
  assign rv_b1 = 0
  assign rv_b2 = 0
  assign rv_b3 = 0
  assign rv_b4 = 0
  assign rv_b5 = 0

  if rv_list.size > 0
    for rv in rv_list
      if rv.hidden.value == true
        continue
      endif
      assign rv_r = rv.rating.value | default: 0 | round
      assign rv_count = rv_count | plus: 1
      assign rv_sum = rv_sum | plus: rv_r
      case rv_r
        when 5
          assign rv_b5 = rv_b5 | plus: 1
        when 4
          assign rv_b4 = rv_b4 | plus: 1
        when 3
          assign rv_b3 = rv_b3 | plus: 1
        when 2
          assign rv_b2 = rv_b2 | plus: 1
        when 1
          assign rv_b1 = rv_b1 | plus: 1
      endcase
    endfor
  endif

  assign rv_avg = 0
  if rv_count > 0
    assign rv_avg = rv_sum | times: 10.0 | divided_by: rv_count | round | divided_by: 10.0
  endif

  comment
    `render` arguments do not accept filters, so any composed label is built here first.
  endcomment
  assign rv_avg_label = 'Average rating: ' | append: rv_avg | append: ' out of 5'
-%}

<div
  id="aao-reviews"
  class="aao-reviews"
  style="max-width:{{ rv_max_width }}px;"
  data-aao-mode="metaobjects"
  data-count="{{ rv_count }}"
  data-rating="{{ rv_avg }}"
>
  {%- if rv_count == 0 -%}
    <div class="aao-reviews__header">
      <div class="aao-reviews__summary">
        <span class="aao-reviews__summary-text"><span>Be the first to review this product</span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="aao-reviews__actions">
        <button type="button" class="aao-reviews__btn" data-aao-write>Write a review</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    <h2 class="aao-reviews__seo">{{ rv_heading }}</h2>

    <div class="aao-reviews__header" data-dist-open="false">
      <div class="aao-reviews__summary">
        <button type="button" class="aao-reviews__summary-btn" aria-expanded="false" data-aao-dist>
          <span class="aao-reviews__summary-stars">
            {%- render 'aao-review-stars', rating: rv_avg, label: rv_avg_label -%}
          </span>
          <span class="aao-reviews__summary-text">
            <span>{{ rv_count }} Review{% unless rv_count == 1 %}s{% endunless %}</span>
            <span class="aao-reviews__chevron"><svg width="14" height="8" viewBox="0 0 14 8" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.11098 5.15691L2.16098 0.206909L0.746979 1.62091L7.11098 7.98491L13.475 1.62091L12.061 0.206911L7.11098 5.15691Z" fill="currentColor"/></svg></span>
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="aao-reviews__actions">
        <button type="button" class="aao-reviews__btn" data-aao-write>Write a review</button>
      </div>

      <div class="aao-reviews__dist">
        {%- comment -%} [loox] the distribution panel shows ONE star followed by the average, at 32px. {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="aao-reviews__dist-avg" role="figure" aria-label="Average rating: {{ rv_avg }} out of 5">
          <svg class="aao-star" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" style="--aao-star-pct:100%"><path class="aao-star__fill" fill="currentColor" d="M24 9.425c0 .212-.125.443-.375.693l-5.236 5.105 1.24 7.212c.01.067.015.164.015.289a.85.85 0 0 1-.151.511.51.51 0 0 1-.44.21c-.183 0-.375-.058-.577-.174L12 19.869l-6.476 3.404c-.212.115-.404.173-.577.173-.202 0-.353-.07-.454-.21a.85.85 0 0 1-.152-.511c0-.058.01-.154.03-.289l1.24-7.211-5.25-5.106C.12 9.858 0 9.628 0 9.425c0-.355.27-.577.808-.663l7.24-1.053 3.245-6.562c.183-.395.418-.592.707-.592s.524.197.707.592l3.245 6.562 7.24 1.053c.539.086.808.308.808.663Z"/></svg>
          <span>{{ rv_avg }}</span>
        </span>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            {%- for rv_s in (1..5) reversed -%}
              {%- liquid
                case rv_s
                  when 5
                    assign rv_n = rv_b5
                  when 4
                    assign rv_n = rv_b4
                  when 3
                    assign rv_n = rv_b3
                  when 2
                    assign rv_n = rv_b2
                  else
                    assign rv_n = rv_b1
                endcase
                assign rv_pct = rv_n | times: 100.0 | divided_by: rv_count
                assign rv_s_label = rv_s | append: ' stars'
              -%}
              <tr
                class="aao-reviews__dist-row"
                data-rating="{{ rv_s }}"
                role="button"
                tabindex="0"
                aria-pressed="false"
                {% if rv_n == 0 %}aria-disabled="true"{% endif %}
                aria-label="Filter by {{ rv_s }} stars, {{ rv_n }} reviews"
              >
                <td>{%- render 'aao-review-stars', rating: rv_s, label: rv_s_label -%}</td>
                <td class="aao-reviews__dist-bar"><div class="aao-reviews__progress"><span style="width:{{ rv_pct }}%"></span></div></td>
                <td class="aao-reviews__dist-count">({{ rv_n }})</td>
              </tr>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Every card is server-rendered. The ones past the first page carry `hidden`; the Load more
      button in assets/aao-reviews-mo.js only clears that attribute, so nothing is fetched and the
      full review text is in the HTML source for crawlers either way. With JavaScript off the
      <noscript> rule below reveals them all and removes the button.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <noscript>
      <style>
        #aao-reviews .aao-review[hidden] { display: flex !important; }
        #aao-reviews .aao-reviews__more,
        #aao-reviews .aao-reviews__dist { display: none !important; }
      </style>
    </noscript>

    <div class="aao-reviews__grid">
      {%- assign rv_i = 0 -%}
      {%- for rv in rv_list -%}
        {%- liquid
          if rv.hidden.value == true
            continue
          endif
          assign rv_i = rv_i | plus: 1
          assign rv_r = rv.rating.value | default: 0 | round
          assign rv_author = rv.author.value | default: 'Anonymous'
          assign rv_photos = rv.photos.value
        -%}
        {%- capture rv_photo_json -%}
          [
          {%- for rv_p in rv_photos -%}
            {%- unless forloop.first %},{% endunless -%}
            {{ rv_p | image_url: width: 1600 | json }}
          {%- endfor -%}
          ]
        {%- endcapture -%}
        <article
          class="aao-review"
          data-rating="{{ rv_r }}"
          {% if rv_photos != blank and rv_photos.size > 0 %}data-photos="{{ rv_photo_json | strip | escape }}"{% endif %}
          {% if rv_i > rv_page_size %}hidden{% endif %}
        >
          <div class="aao-review__main">
            <div class="aao-review__title">
              <span>{{ rv_author | escape }}</span>
              {%- if rv.verified.value == true -%}
                <span class="aao-review__verified"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M12 1.5 14.36 4l3.4-.35.72 3.35 3.02 1.65-1.6 3.03 1.6 3.02-3.02 1.66-.72 3.34-3.4-.34L12 22.5 9.64 20l-3.4.34-.72-3.34-3.02-1.66 1.6-3.02-1.6-3.03L5.52 7l.72-3.35 3.4.35L12 1.5Zm-1.2 13.94 5.68-5.69-1.42-1.41-4.26 4.26-2.14-2.13-1.41 1.41 3.55 3.56Z"/></svg><span>Verified</span></span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

            <div class="aao-review__stars">
              {%- comment -%} the snippet's default label is exactly "<rating> out of 5 stars" {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- render 'aao-review-stars', rating: rv_r -%}
            </div>

            {%- if rv.text.value != blank -%}
              <p class="aao-review__text">{{ rv.text.value | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if rv_photos != blank and rv_photos.size > 0 -%}
              <div class="aao-review__photos">
                {%- for rv_p in rv_photos limit: 4 -%}
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="aao-review__photo"
                    data-photo-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
                    aria-label="Open customer photo {{ forloop.index }}"
                  >
                    <img
                      src="{{ rv_p | image_url: width: 480 }}"
                      alt="Customer photo from {{ rv_author | escape }}"
                      width="480"
                      height="480"
                      loading="lazy"
                      decoding="async"
                    >
                    {%- if forloop.index == 4 and rv_photos.size > 4 -%}
                      <span class="aao-review__photo-more">+{{ rv_photos.size | minus: 3 }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if rv.review_date.value != blank -%}
              <div class="aao-review__time">{{ rv.review_date.value | date: '%-d %B %Y' }}</div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </article>
      {%- endfor -%}

      <p class="aao-reviews__empty" data-aao-empty hidden>No reviews with that rating yet.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="aao-reviews__more" {% if rv_count <= rv_page_size %}hidden{% endif %}>
      <button type="button">Load more reviews</button>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} Crawler-visible plain-text copy, same as seoBlock() in the JS engine. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="aao-reviews__seo">
      <p>{{ rv_product.title | escape }} - rated {{ rv_avg }} out of 5 from {{ rv_count }} customer reviews.</p>
      <ul>
        {%- assign rv_j = 0 -%}
        {%- for rv in rv_list -%}
          {%- liquid
            if rv.hidden.value == true
              continue
            endif
            assign rv_j = rv_j | plus: 1
            if rv_j > rv_jsonld_max
              break
            endif
          -%}
          <li>{{ rv.author.value | default: 'Anonymous' | escape }} - {{ rv.rating.value | default: 0 | round }}/5 - {{ rv.text.value | escape }}</li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  Structured data. Server-rendered, which the JS engine could not do: it injected this after paint,
  so any crawler that does not run JavaScript never saw a rating. Emitted only when there is
  something to say.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if rv_count > 0 -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json" data-aao-reviews>
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org/",
      "@type": "Product",
      "name": {{ rv_product.title | json }},
      "url": {{ shop.url | append: rv_product.url | json }},
      "aggregateRating": {
        "@type": "AggregateRating",
        "ratingValue": {{ rv_avg | json }},
        "reviewCount": {{ rv_count | json }},
        "bestRating": "5",
        "worstRating": "1"
      },
      "review": [
        {%- assign rv_k = 0 -%}
        {%- for rv in rv_list -%}
          {%- liquid
            if rv.hidden.value == true
              continue
            endif
            assign rv_k = rv_k | plus: 1
            if rv_k > rv_jsonld_max
              break
            endif
          -%}
          {%- unless rv_k == 1 %},{% endunless -%}
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": {{ rv.rating.value | default: 0 | round | json }},
              "bestRating": "5",
              "worstRating": "1"
            },
            "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": {{ rv.author.value | default: 'Anonymous' | json }} },
            "datePublished": {{ rv.review_date.value | date: '%Y-%m-%d' | json }},
            "reviewBody": {{ rv.text.value | default: '' | json }}
          }
        {%- endfor -%}
      ]
    }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}
